{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>To You</b> — It has been established that You have an arm. And the meaning: long, so that You can extend it by way of metaphor to wherever You wish, and it is with might. And behold there is no doubt that always, \"Your left hand\" = \"Your right hand will exalt,\" a metaphor of Your two hands."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:27.549018256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}